A narrowed field beneath a struct that a narrow pattern constraint opens: a
copy field by field would drop every field the pattern matches, so the struct
is copied whole, and reported as a whole, as one with ... is.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: "a" | "b"
		[=~"^x"]: string
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: "a"
		[=~"^x"]: string
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		id: v0_0.id
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: "a"
		[=~"^x"]: string
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0358]: the ForwardLens of v1.0 would copy v0_0.meta into meta, which does not accept every value of it
 --> history/1.0.thema:9:1
  |
9 | ForwardLens: {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = note: both v0.0 and v1.0 declare meta, so a lens that does not map it copies it
  = note: meta.owner in v1.0 was "b" and is now "a"
  = help: map meta in the ForwardLens: a _match, a computed value, or a constant
